 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Talk to locals. Ask restaurant staff or hotel kitchens who they recommend. They' often know places that aren't crowded. It' one of the best tips ever. Another is search for a kitchen or chef's table rather than a restaurant. Go straight for the owner. Ask to sit with the kitchen team where food is already cooking. It gives you real taste of a place without waiting. Look for places that cook locally, use fresh ingredients and are owned by friendly people.",
